rt</div><h2>Buildings worth exploring</h2><p class="intro">A few different office environments can help clarify what suits your business. These are starting points for research, not confirmed available spaces.</p><div class="twocol"><article class="building"><div class="type">Traditional downtown tower</div><h3>555 California Street</h3><p>Worth comparing if your business prefers a prominent downtown office setting and convenient access for clients.</p><div class="bottom"><a class="textlink" href="/commercial-real-estate/building/CA/san-francisco/555-california-st/">View building profile →</a></div></article><article class="building"><div class="type">Historic office character</div><h3>Mills Building · 220 Montgomery</h3><p>An alternative to a conventional tower, with historic architecture and a different workplace feel.</p><div class="bottom"><a class="textlink" href="/commercial-real-estate/building/CA/san-francisco/220-montgomery-st/">View building profile →</a></div></article><article class="building"><div class="type">Market Street office</div><h3>425 Market Street</h3><p>Another downtown option to investigate if location and access along Market Street are important to your search.</p><div class="bottom"><a class="textlink" href="/commercial-real-estate/building/CA/san-francisco/425-market-st/">View building profile →</a></div></article></div></section><section class="section"><div class="eyebrow">Compare nearby</div><h2>Other areas worth exploring</h2><p class="intro">If you're considering the Financial District, these nearby areas offer useful contrasts.</p><div class="alternatives"><article class="alt"><h3>Jackson Square</h3><p>Smaller historic buildings and a more intimate setting for businesses that value workplace character.</p><a class="textlink" href="/commercial-real-estate/CA/san-francisco/jackson-square/">Explore district →</a></article><article class="alt"><h3>SoMa</h3><p>A broader range of building types and workplace settings beyond the traditiona